[ system ]
{# ══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
   ONE LINE AT A WEDDING, JUDGED (2.5; native/src/Ceremony.cpp). The DLL runs
   the ceremony as a script and asks this of a line in two ways:
   - ceremony_mode "answer": someone was asked "do you take...?" and this is
     what they said. YES moves the wedding on, NO ends it, UNCLEAR asks again.
   - ceremony_mode "check": did this line do what its step needs (ask for the
     vows, speak them, ask the question, pronounce them married)? Only YES
     counts; anything else and the speaker is cued to do it.
   Rendered with ceremony_mode, ceremony_speaker, ceremony_question and
   ceremony_answer (PublicSendCustomPromptToLLM). [ system ] and [ user ]
   markers are required: without them the messages array is empty.
   ══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════ #}
{% if ceremony_mode == "check" %}
You read one line spoken at a wedding and answer one question about it. Reply with exactly one word: YES or NO.

- YES: the line plainly does what the question asks, in any words.
- NO: it does not - it only praises, comments, waits, or does something else.
{% else %}
You judge one answer at a wedding. Reply with exactly one word: YES, NO or UNCLEAR.

- YES: they agreed, in any words - "I do", "I will", "yes", "with all my heart", or vows that plainly accept.
- NO: they refused, said not yet, said they cannot, or backed away.
- UNCLEAR: anything else - a joke, a question, a change of subject, or words that neither accept nor refuse.
{% endif %}

[ user ]
{% if ceremony_mode == "check" %}
At a wedding, {{ ceremony_speaker }} said: "{{ ceremony_answer }}"

{{ ceremony_question }} One word: YES or NO.
{% else %}
At a wedding, {{ ceremony_speaker }} was asked: "{{ ceremony_question }}"

{{ ceremony_speaker }} answered: "{{ ceremony_answer }}"

Did {{ ceremony_speaker }} say yes? One word: YES, NO or UNCLEAR.
{% endif %}
